WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
Listen. «Je joue».

2
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:06.010
I play. English makes that
negative with one extra word,

3
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:07.510
in front of the verb:

4
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.120
I don't play.

5
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.050
French does something
stranger with its 'not'.

6
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.080
And it doesn't stop at 'not'.

7
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.110
Someone knocks. «Qui est là ?» The answer:

8
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:20.710
«Personne». Nobody. One word on its own.

9
00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:24.770
So why does French wrap 'not'
round the verb like a sandwich,

10
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.590
and what else can go in it?

11
00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:31.290
In this mission, you'll build the
negative sandwich and swap its slices.

12
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.570
Then you'll find out what goes inside it,

13
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.590
and build your own in the lab.

14
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.350
Your mission: work out the sandwich rule.
